{
  "dom_id": "step-q75235",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14247490/assets/293e79685a3f4da205d986bcf4331e4b4f43c0a48fe183d27f93aaee6bb17b99.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+4{m}_{12}+4{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14247490/assets/12df172e3a2f60a8b123937600d5774508ac8cb204696414690490be8d9e2c32.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14247490/assets/b5e72e970d512740cc0d5de9e2d5739d71fb0c90e750c9874042ff4fa5230db9.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(0,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(0,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =4\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
